Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(serve): build the all-profiles project tree at boot,
 after the kanban annotation prewarm [daveey]

After b4f69efc705 fixed the board routes, the first GET /api/profiles/projects/tree after the 22:25Z hub restart
still took 4.02 s (loop-watch), past the Desktop's 4-5 s budget. The first tree build in a new process pays the lazy
tui_gateway.server import, one git root probe per session cwd and every profile's cold annotation scope: ~3 s
uncontended on hermes-hub vs ~0.15-0.4 s warm, and it paid them inside the reconnect burst.

The boot prewarm thread now builds the tree through the route's single-flight cache right after the annotation, so
a poll arriving mid-build waits for it and then reads warm caches. Same daemon thread, no new one; skipped under
HERMES_TEST_ISOLATION as before. (t_01a19864fc42f5b2)
